# Repository-wide ignore rules.
#
# This file is tracked deliberately. A previous revision listed `.gitignore`
# among its own patterns, which meant the file never entered the repository and
# every clone started with no rules at all — the personal data and scan output
# below were then one `git add -A` away from being published. See SECURITY.md.
#
# `app/.gitignore` holds the rules that are specific to the Python project;
# keep application concerns there and repository concerns here.

# --- Personal data ----------------------------------------------------------
# The operator's CV, the collected postings, and any exported extract of them.
# These are personal data under the operator's control (see NOTICE.md) and must
# never be committed, on any branch.
data/
*.cv.txt
cv.txt

# Environment files carry the local database credentials and paths. Only the
# template is tracked.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# --- Raw AI transcripts -----------------------------------------------------
# Docs/AI-LOGS holds unredacted model conversation logs kept for local
# provenance. The whole directory is excluded, summaries included: a summary
# written alongside a transcript has not been reviewed for disclosure. To
# publish one of those notes, move it into Docs/design/ as reviewed prose.
AI-LOGS/
*.jsonl

# --- Secret-scanning output -------------------------------------------------
# TruffleHog writes findings, including the matched secret values, to disk.
# Committing a scan report publishes exactly what the scan exists to catch.
trufflehog-out.json
trufflehog-*.json
.trufflehog-report/

# --- Local agent and scaffolding tooling ------------------------------------
# Not shipped: `.claude/skills/` vendors third-party skill copies, and CLAUDE.md
# plus `.specify/` describe one maintainer's local workflow. The conventions
# they encode are published in CONTRIBUTING.md instead, which is the file
# contributors are expected to read.
.claude/
CLAUDE.md
.specify/

# --- Python -----------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/

# --- Tooling caches ---------------------------------------------------------
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# --- Scratch output ---------------------------------------------------------
*.csv

# --- Editors and operating systems ------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
